<% content_for(:title) { "About" } %>
<% content_for(:description) { "Learn why Civic Gallery exists, how it handles public records, and where to follow the project." } %>
<% content_for :body_class, "atlas-shell" %>
<% content_for :head do %>
  <%= stylesheet_link_tag "atlas", "data-turbo-track": "reload" %>
<% end %>

<main class="atlas-wrap" id="main">
  <%= render "public/shared/atlas_topbar" %>

  <header class="atlas-about-header">
    <p class="atlas-eyebrow">About Civic Gallery</p>
    <h1>Public records<br><em>deserve a better map.</em></h1>
    <p>
      Civic Gallery makes local public records easier to find, follow, and verify.
      It organizes meetings, matters, and documents, while keeping the official
      public record in view as the source of truth.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="atlas-about-grid" aria-label="About Civic Gallery">
    <article>
      <h2>Source-first by design</h2>
      <p>
        This site helps people navigate records published by <%= current_jurisdiction.name %>.
        It links back to the source system and distinguishes official records,
        extracted document text, and generated summaries. Those assistive layers
        can make a record easier to explore; they are not a substitute for it.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h2>For agents and developers</h2>
      <p>
        Civic Gallery offers a supported, read-only <a href="<%= api_v1_documentation_url %>">public API</a>
        and remote MCP endpoint for finding and verifying records. Both retain
        source links and the same provenance boundaries used on the site.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h2>Follow the work</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="https://notes.civicgallery.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Civic Gallery Notes ↗</a>
        is where we write about the project, its experiments, and the questions
        that come up while building public-interest civic software.
      </p>
      <p>
        Start with <a href="https://notes.civicgallery.org/posts/introducing-civic-gallery/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Introducing Civic Gallery ↗</a>,
        or read <a href="https://www.davidalexmcclain.com/coding/civic-gallery" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the technical project notes ↗</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <%= render "public/shared/atlas_footer" %>
</main>
